Chapter 10. Verification Technology

10.1 Detection rate

Suppose the evaluator runs $m$ independent tests on a holdout of $n$ learners. Under gaming intensity $g$, the standardized test statistic is

z = \frac{q \cdot g \cdot \sqrt{m n}}{\sigma_\eta}.

The parameter $q > 0$ is the gaming detectability — distinct from $h_g$. The metric security ratio is

\rho_M = \frac{q}{h_g}.

Regime Interpretation
$\rho_M \gg 1$ Verification amplifies gaming signal
$\rho_M \approx 1$ Same instrument for both
$\rho_M \ll 1$ Verification blind to gaming

10.2 Detection function

Postulate 10.2.1. The detection probability is exponential:

p(g) = 1 - e^{-\kappa g}, \qquad \kappa = \frac{q \sqrt{m n}}{\sigma_\eta z_\alpha},

where $z_\alpha$ is the critical value of the test at significance level $\alpha$ under a one-sided exponential-tail approximation.

This is a modeling choice. The exact power function of a test depends on the alternative distribution. The exponential form is analytically tractable and asymptotically motivated.

10.3 Verification cost

Fix $m$ and $\alpha$. Solve for $n$ given a target $\kappa$:

n(\kappa) = \left( \frac{\kappa \sigma_\eta z_\alpha}{q \sqrt{m}} \right)^2.

Assume linear cost $C_{\mathrm{ver}}(n, m) = c_0 + c_1 m n$. Substituting:

C_{\mathrm{ver}}(\kappa) = c_0 + \frac{c_1 \sigma_\eta^2 z_\alpha^2}{q^2} \kappa^2.

Definition 10.3.1. The verification cost parameter is

c_{\mathrm{test}} := \frac{c_1 \sigma_\eta^2 z_\alpha^2}{q^2}.

Proposition 10.3.2. Under the exponential detection postulate and linear holdout cost,

C_{\mathrm{ver}}(\kappa) = c_0 + c_{\mathrm{test}} \kappa^2.

Proof. Direct substitution. $\square$

Corollary 10.3.3. $c_{\mathrm{test}}$ decreases in $q$ and increases in $\sigma_\eta$, $z_\alpha$, $c_1$. Higher detectability reduces the cost of achieving a target detection rate.

10.4 Comparative statics

Parameter $c_{\mathrm{test}}$ $\kappa_{\mathrm{crit}}$ IC effect
$q \uparrow$ $\downarrow$ unchanged easier IC
$h_g \uparrow$ unchanged $\uparrow$ harder IC
$\sigma_\eta \uparrow$ $\uparrow$ unchanged costlier
$\lambda \uparrow$ unchanged $\downarrow$ easier IC
$s \uparrow$ unchanged $\downarrow$ easier IC

