Appendix H. Proofs for Chapter 12: Endogeneity

H.1 Proof of Theorem D1

Statement. If the provider chooses $h_g \in [h_g^{\min}, \infty)$ while $q$ is fixed, then for any $\Xi_0 > 0$, there exists $h_g^*$ such that $h_g > h_g^*$ implies $\Xi < 1$.

Proof. In the benchmark, $\Xi(h_g) = \Lambda q^2/h_g^2$.

$\Xi(h_g) < 1 \iff h_g^2 > \Lambda q^2 \iff h_g > q\sqrt{\Lambda}$.

Take $h_g^* = q\sqrt{\Lambda}$. Then for $h_g > h_g^*$, $\Xi < 1$. $\square$

H.2 Proof of Theorem D2

Statement. If the provider chooses $q \in (0, q^{\max}]$ while $h_g$ is fixed, then $q \to 0$ implies $\Xi \to 0$.

Proof. $\Xi(q) = \Lambda q^2/h_g^2$, strictly increasing in $q$. As $q \to 0$, $\Xi \to 0$. $\square$

