Appendix N. Summary of Key Inequalities

The following inequalities are used throughout and are proven above.

(N.1) $f(u) = e^{-2u} - 1 + 2u e^{-u} < 0$ for all $u > 0$. (Lemma A.2.1)

(N.2) $\partial D/\partial \kappa(g, \kappa) < 0$ for all $g > 0$, $\kappa > 0$. (Theorem B)

(N.3) $R'(u) < 0$ for all $u > 0$, $\eta > 0$. (Lemma K.2.1)

(N.4) $F'(u) < 0$ for all $u \in (0, 1)$, $r \in (0, 1)$, $\eta > 0$. (Lemma K.5.1)

(N.5) $e_0 - e^*(g) \leq \lambda s \kappa g/m_e$ under $C_e'' \geq m_e$. (Lemma K.7.1)

(N.6) $C_g'(g) \geq m_g g$ under $C_g'' \geq m_g$ and $C_g'(0) = 0$. (Lemma K.6.1)

(N.7) $1 - e^{-x} \leq x$ for $x \geq 0$. (Lemma K.1.1)

(N.8) $U''(0) = -c_g$ for quadratic costs at the boundary. (Lemma K.4.1)

(N.9) $\mathcal{L}(\kappa) \sim \mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{L}}(\kappa_{\mathrm{crit}} - \kappa)$ with $\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{L}} = (v - \lambda)\lambda^2 s^2 h_g/(c_e c_g)$. (Lemma K.9.1)

